# Git worktrees (not stash)

Parallel streams live in **separate checkouts**. Do not `git stash` as the primary way to switch between UI experiments and production hotfixes — stash is fragile and lossy.

## Layout

| Path | Branch | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `/Users/ganeshsp/Projects/webinar` | `main` | Clean production / hotfixes / deploys |
| `/Users/ganeshsp/Projects/webinar-ui` | `feat/ui-simplify` | UI redesign, preview auth-bypass, experiments |

```bash
# List worktrees
git worktree list

# Add another stream (example)
git worktree add -b feat/my-experiment /Users/ganeshsp/Projects/webinar-my-experiment main
```

## Agent rules

- **Hotfixes / deploys:** work in `webinar` on `main` (or a short-lived hotfix branch off `main` in that tree).
- **UI / experiments:** work in `webinar-ui` on `feat/ui-simplify` (or another feature worktree).
- **Deploy** from the worktree that contains the change you intend to ship.
- **Never** stash redesign work just to free `main` for a hotfix — use the other worktree.
- One-time `stash` only to *move* dirty files into a new worktree, then drop it.
- Do not force-push. Do not skip hooks.

## Localhost (UI redesign)

From the UI worktree (API/Postgres/LiveKit can already be up from `main`):

```bash
cd /Users/ganeshsp/Projects/webinar-ui
./start.sh                 # full stack from this tree
# or frontend only if API/SFU already healthy:
cd web && npm run dev      # http://localhost:3000
```

Copy gitignored env if missing: `web/.env.local`, `web/.dev.vars` from the main checkout. Preview bypass routes live under `/preview` on this branch only.
